The Cellar Crawl
Seven rooms under an old vineyard. Find the bottle; keep hold of the light.

> look
Foot of the Cellar Stairs
Worn steps climb back up toward the daylight. The air is cold and smells of oak.
Exits: north

> go up
You cannot go that way.

> go sideways
"sideways" is not a direction.

> go north
The Barrel Hall
Fat oak barrels sweat in the gloom. A trapdoor is set into the flagstones.
Exits: south, east, west, down (locked)

> go down
That way is locked. You need the brass key.

> unlock down
The lock will not turn without the brass key.

> go west
The Cooperage
Staves, iron hoops, and a half-built barrel. A cooper's bench runs along the wall.
Here: a brass key
Exits: east

